The attached image (Fig. 4) illustrates the active transport of Nano-11 nanoparticles to the draining lymph node by antigen-presenting cells (APCs) following intramuscular injection. Panel A and B show that the percentage of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells in the lymph node peaks at day 2 (3.5%) and subsequently decreases by day 7. Panel C demonstrates that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) consistently comprise the largest fraction (60-80%) of Nano-11-positive cells. Panel D further indicates that MigDCs exhibit the highest mean fluorescence intensity, signifying a greater uptake of Nano-11 per cell compared to other APC subtypes, supporting Nano-11's efficient targeting to immunopotentiating MigDCs.